# Repositories

```kotlin
// ✅ existing pattern
override suspend fun getFoo(): Result<Foo> {
    val network = ApiCallHandler.safeCall {
        api.getFoo().mrData./* … */.also { saveCache(CacheKeys.FOO, it, FooModel::class.java) }
    }
    return network.map { it.toDomain() }
        .recoverCatching { peekFooCache() ?: throw it }
}

override suspend fun peekFooCache(): Foo? =
    loadCache(CacheKeys.FOO, FooModel::class.java)?.toDomain()
```

- Expose work through `IF1Repository` / `IEspnRepository`; bind impls in `RepositoryModule`.
- Wrap all network in `ApiCallHandler.safeCall` → `Result`. Map DTOs → domain via `data/mapper` (`toDomain`, etc.).
- Jolpica: Room key-value (`CacheKeys` + `CacheJsonMapper`); pair every cached `get*` with `peek*Cache`.
- ESPN: in-memory TTL caches inside `EspnRepository` — do not push ESPN into `F1Repository` or Room unless asked.
- Parsing and HTTP stay here; ViewModels only consume `Result` / peek. Update the interface + Hilt bind together when adding methods.
